#include <hexi/static_buffer.h>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdint>

template<size_t buffer_size = 1024>
void write_data_to_buffer(hexi::static_buffer<std::byte, buffer_size>& buffer, const std::vector<uint8_t>& data) {
    buffer.write(data.data(), data.size());
}

template<size_t buffer_size = 1024>
std::vector<uint8_t> read_data_from_buffer(hexi::static_buffer<std::byte, buffer_size>& buffer, size_t bytes_to_read) {
    std::vector<uint8_t> result(bytes_to_read);
    buffer.read(result.data(), bytes_to_read);
    return result;
}
```

## Explanation:

**`write_data_to_buffer` function:**
- Uses the `write(const void* source, size_type length)` method from `static_buffer`
- Passes `data.data()` to get a pointer to the vector's data
- Passes `data.size()` to specify how many bytes to write
- The buffer's write method will copy the data and advance the write cursor

**`read_data_from_buffer` function:**
- Creates a `std::vector<uint8_t>` with the requested size
- Uses the `read(void* destination, size_type length)` method from `static_buffer`
- Passes `result.data()` as the destination buffer
- Passes `bytes_to_read` to specify how many bytes to read
- The buffer's read method will copy the data and advance the read cursor
- Returns the populated vector

Both functions properly handle the type conversion between `std::byte` (used internally by the buffer) and `uint8_t` (used in the API) through implicit pointer conversions to `void*`.

